course: dictionary
lesson: 3067
title: Words from science and everyday life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ecosystem is all the living things in one place, such as plants, animals, fungi and tiny germs, together with the non-living things around them, like water, soil, air and sunlight. Everything in it affects everything else.
explain: Look at the context: «A wild beaver family on the River Otter in Devon was allowed to stay in 2020; beaver dams slow rivers, hold water in droughts, reduce flooding downstream and make ponds full of wildlife.» The clues are dams, rivers, ponds and wildlife. The beavers change the water and land, and the animals and plants around them change too. That whole connected web is the ecosystem.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. A group of apps, phones and computers that work closely together can be called a tech ecosystem. The words around it tell you which meaning fits: a pond full of wildlife, or products that work together.
fact: An ecosystem is all the living things in one place, together with the non-living things around them, like water, soil, air and sunlight.
fact: «Ecosystem engineers» are animals that change the land around them, such as beavers.
fact: Beaver dams slow rivers, hold water in droughts and reduce flooding downstream.
fact: A «balanced ecosystem» is one where all its parts work well together.
fact: In everyday talk, a «tech ecosystem» means products that work together.
exercise: What is an ecosystem? | *All the living things in one place, together with the non-living things around them | A type of rock found in rivers | A fast-moving stream | A single animal living alone in a forest
exercise: «Beaver dams slow rivers, hold water in droughts and reduce flooding downstream.» What does this show? | Beavers only eat fish | Rivers never flood | Dams are made of metal | *Beavers change the land and water around them
exercise: «In a tech ecosystem, phones, apps and computers work together.» What does ecosystem mean here? | A school of fish | A type of soil | A pond full of frogs | *A group of products that work closely together
test: Which of these is a non-living part of an ecosystem? | Tiny germ | Mushroom | Fungus | *Soil
test: «Ecosystem engineers» means animals that? | Live in deserts only | *Change the land around them more than most animals | Never move | Only eat other animals
exam: Why are beavers called «ecosystem engineers»? | They build houses in towns | Because they only live in one place | Because they dig for gold | *Because they change the land and water around them a lot
